    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (87.42) standing alone as our premier offensive anchor. Facing a favorable matchup against Fedde, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite 0.477 xwOBA and a significant boost from his prime spot in the two-hole. Alongside him, **Colt Keith** (69.64) and **Trea Turner** (67.40) represent high-ceiling plays; **Colt Keith** is particularly well-positioned, as the combination of his leadoff status and a soft matchup against Avila provides the necessary environment to maximize his run-scoring potential. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (62.83) faces a tougher arm in Ashcraft, his aggressive placement at the top of the order and a favorable platoon advantage keep him firmly in \"Strong\" territory.\n\nStrategic platoon edges and park factors were the primary drivers in our roster construction. **Casey Schmitt** (53.48) received a critical late boost from wind blowing out at his venue, pushing his utility value higher despite an otherwise modest projection. Conversely, the most difficult decision on our bench involved **Carson Benge** (45.90), who served as the final cut. While his metrics were respectable, the crowded nature of our middle infield and outfield tiers left him just outside the threshold for a start today. We have also opted to sit **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, and **Pedro Ramirez** entirely, as their projected efficiencies fell below our 40.0 \"Below Floor\" threshold, prioritizing game cap preservation over their marginal expected contributions.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given several pending lineups. Both **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** carry \"Lineup Pending\" designations against Will Warren; while we have assumed their placement, any fluctuation in their batting order could necessitate a recalibration of our expected run totals. Furthermore, keep an eye on **Caleb Durbin** (58.29); his performance against Gausman is bolstered by a tendency to capitalize on slower pitcher deliveries, a nuance that makes him a high-leverage target for stolen base production today. Owners should monitor weather reports specifically for the games involving **Casey Schmitt** and **Dillon Dingler** to ensure no late-breaking precipitation impacts these favorable park conditions.",
